WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:01.067
This is

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.502
unbelievably sad news,

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.371
especially because many people

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:06.573
just saw her on Tuesday night's

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.640
Golden Globes.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.608
Many tuning in

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.143
because of the first actual award

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.178
ceremony and a couple a couple of years

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.246
and her own father

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:16.649
being memorialized in this hit movie.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.918
What more can you tell us about

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:19.586
that night?

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:21.254
And what's happened?

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.922
Laura, good evening.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.357
I was at the Golden Globes.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.592
I was at the Beverly Hilton

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.694
Hotel in the ballroom, seated

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.562
just a few tables behind

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.731
Lisa Marie and her mother, Priscilla.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:34.034
And I immediately thought to myself

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.168
when I saw her

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.937
that she just didn't look like her

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:41.708
usual glowing bubbly, happy self.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.010
She looked a bit somber.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.211
And I also just want to tell you,

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.346
a few moments ago,

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.882
we received a statement from the family

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:49.716
represent him

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.117
saying that they are shocked

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.352
and devastated

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.987
by the tragic death

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.655
of their beloved Lisa Marie.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.023
And like you said,

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:57.924
as for a statement

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.292
that Priscilla had released

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:00.460
that they are profoundly grateful

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.594
for the support.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.563
Now, this comes as a shock to so many

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.732
because just a few hours ago, Priscilla

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.500
taking to Instagram,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.869
asking for prayers in support,

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:10.770
telling everyone

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.604
that her daughter

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.106
was rushed to the hospital.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.808
We know at CNN

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:15.608
that paramedics

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.544
responded to a call at Lisa

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.412
Marie, his home in Calabasas, California,

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.047
for possible cardiac arrest.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.916
No other details at this time

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.084
as to what happened.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.085
But like you said,

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.420
it was a huge night

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.355
for the Presley family.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.857
Because Baz Luhrmann,

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:31.925
like you said,

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:32.992
immortalizing,

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:36.062
memorializing Elvis, their father,

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:39.432
her husband, Priscilla's husband, on

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.234
screen, Austin Butler doing this

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.769
incredible portrayal

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.003
and taking to the stage

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.772
when he won his Golden Globe

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:48.108
with this emotional speech,

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.110
looking right at the table.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.212
He was sitting with them that evening.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.614
I can only imagine how devastated he is.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:55.381
And we haven't

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.883
heard back from him,

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.284
but we've reached out to Austin Butler

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:58.952
for comment.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:00.420
And at

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.021
one point, it looked like Lisa

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.124
Marie was wiping tears from her eyes.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.992
And we know how much this movie

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:06.893
meant to the family.

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:07.961
And we know how much Lisa

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.662
Marie championed

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.563
Austin Butler

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:11.297
and helped him

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.100
get to know what Elvis really was like.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.503
You heard Stephanie Elam earlier

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.370
with Anderson.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.805
You heard Nischelle Turner

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.373
from Entertainment Tonight earlier,

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.375
who interviewed her as well on the carpet

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.511
saying that something seemed off.

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.211
And I think all of us

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.480
sort of turned to the other and said,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.015
you know, this doesn't seem like her

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.183
usual self.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:30.884
But look, like you

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:33.019
said, it's been a rough couple of years

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.654
losing her son, Benjamin,

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.556
to suicide in 20, 20.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:37.657
She opened up about it

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.392
in an essay in July.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.560
I want to read you a little bit

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.828
of what she said.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:42.529
She said,

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.697
My heart and soul went with you.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.500
The depth of the pain is suffocating.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.735
And bottomless

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:52.438
without you every moment of every day.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:56.776
That is just she loved her son so much.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.344
And like she writes, my heart

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.913
and soul went with you.

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:02.215
Now, we don't know what led to her

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.216
death today,

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.050
but we know it's

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.718
been a profoundly difficult time.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.087
She is survived by three of her

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.222
other children,

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.957
Riley Keough being one of them

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.492
who is an actress.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:14.194
We still have not yet heard from them,

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.562
but this is all just happened

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:16.896
just moments ago.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.665
Again, we just saw her

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:19.899
at the Golden Globes.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.968
It's been a big couple of months

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.770
for the family with Austin Butler

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.605
and all the rave reviews

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.140
for Baz Luhrmann's Elvis.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.308
And this was you know,

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.275
we were about to

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.411
you're about to have Oscar nominations.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.380
This movie is definitely, in my opinion,

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.248
going to be nominated

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.183
also and going to be nominated

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:39.152
know the Oscars are in March.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.920
And this would have been a huge moment

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.323
for the family to be there together.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:46.593
And now this sadness, another tragedy

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.127
that the Presley family

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:51.030
is so used to facing tragedy and grief

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.966
in such a public way.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:53.733
Chloe, thank you.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.034
And again, a mother

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.003
with surviving children as well.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:59.739
What a devastating blow to this family.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.708
I want to bring in Sharon Waxman, editor

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.276
in chief of The Wrap.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:07.280
Sharon, so many people remember and know

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.315
and are familiar with Lisa Marie Presley

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.017
across multiple generations.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.151
You have those who remembered

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.120
when she was the young apple

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.154
and apple of the eye

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.322
and twinkle in the

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.657
I have an Elvis Presley

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:18.992
and a young Priscilla.

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:21.027
People recall from generations

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:21.961
of my own included

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.897
when she was married to Michael Jackson.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.933
Another actor, Nicholas Cage, as well.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.234
I mean, the idea of many people

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:29.135
in different generations

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:29.802
knowing her

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.104
and then learning about her,

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:33.406
even in her really open way

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:33.873
of talking

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.842
about the grief that she experienced

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:38.077
and 20, 20 at the loss of her son's life.

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:40.813
She has been in the public eye

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.782
and here we are

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.851
learning that she has died.

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.753
What is the reaction that you

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:47.320
were hearing

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:50.356
Well, I think people are

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.325
really shocked in Hollywood

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:54.193
and we're just seeing an outpouring

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.129
of exactly that.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:56.529
First of all,

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:57.997
there were people who, of course,

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:02.201
just saw her this one of the new new laid

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:03.836
back in-person

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:06.706
events at the Golden Globes Awards.

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.641
Seasons have just been so muted

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.143
in the past few years.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.311
And so this year,

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.779
Elvis is one of the movies

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:15.782
that's really celebratory and brings

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:19.085
to light to going back to the movies.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:21.254
And it was interesting,

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:23.690
in fact, that the movie was backed

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.226
by the family that they were supporting,

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:27.860
was learning

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.062
the director,

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:30.630
that they watched the film

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.931
all together with them

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:32.999
for the first time

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:36.269
ahead of the movie's release, of course.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.205
So it's really shock.

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:41.641
I think that you're going to be hearing

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:43.443
already that story

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.478
on the side that reflects

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:47.246
all across entertainment

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:49.048
And Sharon, I mean,

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:52.018
she was just nine years old herself

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:54.220
when her father, Elvis, died.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.490
And in many respects, it seemed as though

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:58.991
she considered herself

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:01.928
a bit of a caretaker of his legacy.

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:03.363
Is that right?

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:04.964
Yeah, I think so.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:05.665
And Priscilla,

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:08.201
her mother, of course, as well,

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:10.837
I remember talking to Lisa Marie's

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:12.538
daughter, Riley, at the Cannes

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:13.973
Film Festival this year.

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:15.341
Riley is followed

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:17.310
in the family footsteps

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.412
in going into entertainment.

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.146
She's an actress,

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.714
