00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:36.115
To support Austin Butler, who she did

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:37.817
care for a great deal

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:40.319
and was so happy with his portrayal of

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:43.055
of her father to support Baz Luhrmann,

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:44.423
who was also was

00:08:44.423 --> 00:08:46.125
the director, was also nominated

00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:47.159
for a Golden Globe.

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:49.929
So it was going to be a celebratory night

00:08:50.296 --> 00:08:50.897
for them.

00:08:50.897 --> 00:08:51.797
They had also just

00:08:51.797 --> 00:08:53.799
celebrated her father's birthday

00:08:53.799 --> 00:08:55.234
a couple of days before.

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:57.503
So she talked about that as well

00:08:57.503 --> 00:08:58.838
and about how special of a night

00:08:58.838 --> 00:08:59.338
it would be

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:00.840
because they were celebrating her

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:01.941
father's birthday,

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:03.943
celebrating the success of the film.

00:09:03.943 --> 00:09:05.945
And the actress portrayal of her father.

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:08.180
But she did not seem to be

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.649
her her normal self.

